 "findings": [
  {
   "evidence": "In `TauCeti/Topology/VectorBundle/Subbundle.lean:149`, `IsSubbundleFrameOn` includes `linearIndependent` and `span_eq ... = V x`, so `V x` has a basis indexed by `\u03b9`. That basis is used as `hX.basis hx` in `TotallyReal/Trivialization.lean:95`. `bundleDiffeomorph` (`Hom.lean:615`) requires only `[FiniteDimensional \ud835\udd5c F\u2081]` for the source model.",
   "file": "TauCeti/Geometry/Manifold/VectorBundle/ComplementarySubbundle.lean",
   "fix": "Remove `[FiniteDimensional \ud835\udd5c F]` from the section variables. In `hfib`, get finite-dimensionality of `V x` and `W x` from the local frames (`IsSubbundleFrameOn.basis` at `x`, via `hV x` / `hW x`), and get `T2Space` from `e.toHomeomorph` as now. Update the docstrings and module doc that say 'with finite-dimensional model fibre'.",
   "issue": "The `IsCompl` section variable `[FiniteDimensional \ud835\udd5c F]` is not needed, so `exists_bundleDiffeomorph_prod_of_isCompl` and `contMDiff_totalSpace_projectionOnto_of_isCompl` are stated more narrowly than necessary. The proof uses it only in `hfib`, to get `FiniteDimensional (V x \u00d7 W x)` through `E x`. That already follows because `V x` and `W x` have bases indexed by the finite types `\u03b9` and `\u03b9'`. `T2Space (E x)` comes from the trivialization homeomorphism with the normed space `F`, which needs no finite dimension. `bundleDiffeomorph` only needs a finite-dimensional source model, `(\u03b9 \u2192 \ud835\udd5c) \u00d7 (\u03b9' \u2192 \ud835\udd5c)`, and that holds automatically.",
   "line": 105
  }
 ],
